candidates.demonstrated_gap:
The candidate is the `browse` package in packages/cli (npm latest 0.11.1, MIT), not the Stagehand SDK. The SDK needs an LLM key for act and extract (its README example passes OPENAI_API_KEY), which would duplicate the native client's agent loop. `browse` belongs to agent-browser's class:
- a per-session daemon that keeps cookies, tabs and snapshot refs (@0-12) between invocations;
- 30+ DOM commands, network and console telemetry, --json output and `browse doctor`;
- a managed local browser by default (BROWSERBASE_API_KEY only selects remote), plus --auto-connect and --cdp.
No measured comparison with agent-browser exists, and agent-browser already covers this surface, so no requirement gap is demonstrated today. Its browse.sh site-skills catalog ('browse skills add apartments.com') is community-authored, which makes it an untrusted-instruction surface. Whether the CLI sends its own usage telemetry is unverified; only the README was read. Maintenance: 23 commits under packages/cli since 2026-07-07, including release commit 8008208122 ('Release browse@0.11.1 (#3041)', 2026-09-30). The newest browse GitHub release is browse@0.9.6 (2026-08-03); the repository's latest GitHub release is @browserbasehq/stagehand@3.7.3 (2026-08-28).

Re-judged on v0.9.4 (2026-09-23). The decisive reason is requirement fit. The layer defines no crawl or ingestion task, so its overturn_when ('a defined source-coverage or ingestion task exceeds the current commands') is unmet. Page extraction is already covered by agent-browser plus the trafilatura survivor (v2.3.0, 2026-10-02). What is new in 0.9.x is speed, not attributable coverage: content pruning is about 10x faster with the lxml-native PruningContentFilterLXML, now the default. The supply-chain facts are secondary:
- the GitHub Advisory Database lists 13 reviewed crawl4ai advisories;
- 10 of their summaries name the Docker server or API, and GHSA-r253-r9jw-qg44's description scopes it to the Docker API's request-supplied extra_args;
- GHSA-2jq4-q6vv-4cp3 (critical, path traversal in crawler downloads) also reached SDK users who crawled an attacker-controlled page before 0.9.0;
- GHSA-445m-27cf-gr3x affects 0.4.247 and earlier;
- none version-matches 0.9.4.
The 0.9.4 CHANGELOG separately names three more fixed advisories, described in Docker-server terms, which the database query did not return: GHSA-f77g-77vp-r96v, GHSA-wh5w-hmj3-vgg7 and GHSA-5w5p-vcv6-mm3f. Maintenance is active (default-branch commit 2026-10-05).
